## What "Complete the feature" Means in This Version

For every feature area below, "complete" means: **the UI is fully wired to realistic hardcoded JSON and behaves correctly against that static data**, not that it talks to a real backend.

### Authentication
Simulate login/logout/session state client-side using a hardcoded user object from `students.json`. Protected routes should check local simulated session state, not a real token.

### Student Profile
Full profile editing UI works against local state seeded from JSON; "saving" updates local state only.

### Universities / Courses
Browse, search, filter, save/unsave, compare — all operating over the static `universities.json` / `courses.json` arrays with client-side filtering logic (no server-side search).

> Per the original product requirement: Course Search should **not** appear on the student dashboard/navigation. Keep the course data and any search logic available in the `data/` and component layer (not deleted), but do not surface it in the dashboard UI.

### Applications
Create/edit application, document upload (simulate file selection and store metadata only, no real upload), status, timeline, milestones, deadlines — all against local state derived from `applications.json`.

### Document Management
Upload/delete/replace/preview/download simulated against local state; no real file storage.

### Appointments
View/request/reschedule/cancel using `appointments.json` + local state. This remains the dashboard card that replaces "Visa Application" (see below).

### Notifications
Unread count, mark read/mark all read, history — all derived from `notifications.json` and local state (no real-time/websocket integration).

### Progress Tracking / Ignition Points
Compute displayed percentages/points **client-side** from the static milestone/points JSON so the numbers look dynamic and reactive to on-screen actions, but there is no server-side points engine.

### Activity Feed / Timeline
Rendered from `activityFeed.json`; new simulated actions (e.g. clicking "complete task") can prepend a locally-generated entry to local state for realism.

### AI Interview Module
UI flow (start, answer questions, continue, complete, see score/feedback) runs entirely against hardcoded question sets and hardcoded/randomized-but-static feedback in `interviews.json` / `interviewFeedback.json`. Do not call any real AI/model API.

### Student Task & Checklist Engine
Render the milestone chain (Passport → IELTS → SOP → LOR → Apply → Interview → Offer → Visa → Departure) from `tasksChecklist.json`, with due dates/dependencies encoded in the JSON and completion toggled in local state.

### Counsellor Visibility
If counsellor-facing views exist, render them from the same static datasets (e.g. `students.json`, `ignitionPoints.json`) — read-only or locally-editable, no backend writes.

